meta {
  name: Sync Agent Nodes
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

put {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/workspaces/:workspace/agents/:agent/nodes
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  workspace: 1
  agent: 1
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "nodes": [
      {
        "node_id": 1,
        "config": { "channel": "#alerts" },
        "exposed_fields": ["text"]
      },
      {
        "node_id": 2
      }
    ]
  }
}

docs {
  Replaces the set of nodes the agent may call as tools (pass `nodes: []` to detach
  all). Every `node_id` must be a builtin catalog node or a custom node in this
  workspace.

  Each attachment may pin part of the node's config so the model cannot choose it:

  - `config` fixes values (a credential, a Slack channel). Bound fields are hidden from
    the model and merged in after whatever it supplies, so they can't be overridden.
  - `exposed_fields` narrows what is left to the arguments worth asking a model to fill.
    Omit it to offer every unbound field.

  A new version is snapshotted when the attached set or its bindings actually change.
  Requires the `agent.nodes.sync` permission.

  Expected result:
  - 200 with the agent's updated nodes.
  - 422 if any `node_id` isn't visible to this workspace.
  - 403 if the user lacks the `agent.nodes.sync` permission.
}
